A||||9||GT Bastard||Where can I get a set of hipo hypereutectics?||||1||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||07-06-2000||02:27 PM||||Pistons that is...  Summit and Jegs can only get cast replacements.  Forged are beyond my budget.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||07-06-2000||03:51 PM||||I'm curious why you want them?||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||07-06-2000||05:22 PM||||Tougher than cast, cheaper than forged.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||07-06-2000||08:35 PM||||Try Performance Automotive Warehouse. Beware though there customer service sucks. Also try Northern Auto.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pattyb||07-06-2000||09:18 PM||||Performance Automotive Warehouse has the Federal Mogul Hypereutectic pistons and kits but I think the smallest chevy engine they have is for the 3.8 V6.  If you call they sometimes do special orders.  1-818-678-3000<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||07-07-2000||10:12 AM||||What are all you 3.1 guys using for pistons?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Eric||07-07-2000||01:46 PM||||Call Summit back.  Sometimes if you aren't sure what you need, the guy on the other end will give you a bunch of crap about not having the part or something.  Tell the guy you want Federal Mogul Hypereutectic pistons p# H562CP.  Make sure those check out as '90 or so Firebird/ Camaro replacement pistons.  Don't be confused, the hypereutectic are still cast aluminum, but they are manufactured to be stronger than original pistons.||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||07-07-2000||01:49 PM||||Cool, thanks for the info Eric.  Are those flat-tops?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Eric||07-08-2000||12:34 AM||||No, they're dished.  The compression ratio is about 8.8:1 or so on my engine.  They'll make nearly as much power as flat tops, but you won't have to spend $1000 to get them made.||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT Bastard||07-08-2000||12:37 AM||||Dished is ok.... BUT, I know that nitrous is a big no-no with hypers, so what about boost generated from a turbo?  I was under the understanding that nitrous melts the hypers because of a chemical reaction.  Is this correct?||||reg||1
